;; An index `a[e as usize]` whose `e` is not a number, a `bool` or a `char`: an enum's
;; discriminant used as a position.
;;
;; agents/annoyances/image-part-array-positional-callers.json: crates/hir-def/src/deps/image.rs
;; indexes `parts: [&[u8]; Part::ALL.len()]` by `part as usize`, and `Part::DefMap` held tag 2,
;; the next part's place, so a new part read the def map's bytes. Rule 76 (a value with a
;; meaning is a type: a typed index). `as_cast` reports every `as` and `untyped_index` integer
;; fields; neither says the cast's source is an enum.
;;
;; The type is read by its shape (`type-kind`), so only an enum is found; a raw pointer or a
;; fn item cast to `usize` is an address, not a position, and is left alone.
;;
;; Rule 73: the type is the end (an array keyed by the enum, `[T; N]` behind `Index<Part>`);
;; this lint finds where.

(rule (enum-cast-index i e t) (expr i "$a[$e as usize]") (type-of e t) (type-kind t "enum"))

(lint enum-cast-index warning "indexes by `$e` of type `$t` cast to `usize`: key the array by the type")
